    feat(live-session): backend WS pipeline for live threshold-crossing rationale
    
    Phase B of the unified live-threshold-rationale plan
    (dev/briefs/unified-plan.md). Adds the structural skeleton for the
    end-to-end live trading session: Binance ingest → snapshot → threshold
    detection → dual-path verdict → Claude rationale gated by T3 NLI →
    WebSocket fanout + REST audit replay.
    
    New modules under src/market_risk/live_session/:
    - ws_schemas.py: Pydantic envelopes mirroring @platform/contracts,
      discriminated union on `type`, Decimal-as-string JSON
    - models.py: SQLModel ORM rows for 4 hypertables
    - market_bus.py: bounded asyncio.Queue per subscriber with drop-newest
      backpressure and drop-count metric
    - snapshot_builder.py: Welford sigma, VaR_95 closed-form, VWAP slippage
    - ingestor.py: Binance combined-streams ingestor with ref-counted symbol
      tasks and exponential backoff (websockets dep optional)
    - zone_hash.py: bucketize boundary-relevant scalars to a tuple hash
    - threshold_detector.py: stateful detector, emits on verdict transition
      only, zone-hash fast-path
    - verdict_service.py: dual-path resolver (sync DecisionEngine /
      Temporal ComplianceCheckWorkflow), path chosen at rule-load time
    - nli_gate.py: DeBERTa entailment with deterministic stub fallback
    - rationale_streamer.py: Claude tokens + NLI gate, emits N tokens +
      one terminal envelope (verified or retracted)
    - session_manager.py: per-intent Session lifecycle + monotonic seq
    - ws_handler.py: FastAPI WS route /v2/ws/trade/{intent_id} with
      20s/10s heartbeat
    - audit_service.py: chronological 4-table join keyed by intent_id
    
    Plus:
    - alembic 002 migration creating 4 TimescaleDB hypertables (7-day
      chunks, 90-day retention, guarded so plain Postgres / SQLite test
      DBs work)
    - /audit/{intent_id} REST endpoint registered via audit_router
    - /v2/ws/trade/{intent_id} WS endpoint registered
    - LIVE_THRESHOLD_RATIONALE_ENABLED + LIVE_RATIONALE_DAILY_TOKEN_CAP
      settings in src/config.py (flag defaults off)
    - README.md updated to list the Live Session domain
    
    Tests under tests/market_risk/:
    - test_ws_schemas: envelope round-trip on mock-ws fixtures +
      discriminated-union rejection + Decimal string serialization
    - live_session/test_snapshot_math: Welford determinism, VaR closed-form,
      thin vs deep slippage
    - live_session/test_market_bus: fan-out, backpressure drop counting,
      unsubscribe cleanup, async stream iteration
    - live_session/test_zone_hash: hash determinism, distinct buckets
    - live_session/test_threshold_detector: first-tick suppression, emit
      on transition, fast-path
    - live_session/test_verdict_service: sync compliant/conditional/blocked,
      Temporal dispatch, fallback when executor absent
    - live_session/test_rationale_streamer: token stream -> verified,
      drift -> retracted, stub scorer bounds
    
    Gates:
    - ruff check src/market_risk/live_session/ src/market_risk/ws_schemas.py
      tests/market_risk/ -> clean
    - mypy --strict src/market_risk/live_session/ src/market_risk/ws_schemas.py
      -> success, 14 source files
    - pytest deferred: pre-existing Python 3.14 / FastAPI inspect.signature
      bug (per CLAUDE.md known issues), not in this code.
    
    Follow-up: wire session_manager._consume_forever() to compose
    ingestor + builder + detector + verdict + streamer end-to-end. The
    skeleton accepts connections; the production density of work in the
    consume loop lands in a focused integration session that follows.
    
    See dev/briefs/phase-summaries/B-backend-live-session.md for the full
    work summary.

